## Task Quality Checks

Before presenting any Task, verify:

### Feature Task Checks

- [ ] Description focuses on user-facing behavior
- [ ] Definition of Done includes code, tests, docs, and PR workflow (10+ items typical)
- [ ] File paths are exact and follow project structure (`Assets/Scripts/[Category]/[FileName].cs`)
- [ ] Implementation Notes include algorithm choices and performance considerations
- [ ] Dependencies list specific tasks/systems (with SPWT-X or system names)
- [ ] Risks are implementation-specific and categorized
- [ ] Performance targets included ("<0.5ms for 100 entities")

### Tech Task Checks

- [ ] Technical Objective explains WHAT + WHY with quantifiable improvement
- [ ] Definition of Done includes performance metrics (before/after)
- [ ] Technical Refinement provides step-by-step plan
- [ ] Performance Impact section shows concrete improvement ("10x faster")
- [ ] Rollback strategy included for risky changes
- [ ] Documentation updates included in DoD

### Bug Task Checks

- [ ] Reproduction steps are exact and detailed (any developer can reproduce)
- [ ] Expected vs Actual behavior clearly contrasted
- [ ] Environment info complete (versions, platform, commit hash, reproducibility %)
- [ ] Root Cause Analysis explains WHY (not just WHAT)
- [ ] Regression test required in Definition of Done
- [ ] Fix tested across multiple platforms if applicable

### Universal Task Checks

- [ ] Correct template chosen (Feature/Tech/Bug matches request)
- [ ] All INSTRUCTION/FORMAT/EXAMPLE labels removed
- [ ] Parent Story (SPWS-X) referenced
- [ ] Risks categorized with emoji (🔴🟡🟠🔵)
- [ ] All emoticons and markdown formatting preserved
- [ ] Uses correct Unity/DOTS terminology
- [ ] Written in English
